A '''Transmission Tuner''' is an {{Epic}} {{Rift Transferable}} item. It is unlocked at {{Coll|Enderman Slayer 3}} and drops from the {{MobSprite|Voidgloom Seraph}}.

== Obtaining ==
A '''Transmission Tuner''' is a {{Odds|rare}} drop from {{SlayerTier|3}}+ {{MobSprite|Voidgloom Seraph;Voidgloom Seraphim}}. It is unlocked at {{Coll|Enderman Slayer LVL 3}}. 

;Drop Chances
* {{Stier|3}}: {{Green|2.24%}} ({{Green|1}}/{{Yellow|44.73}})
* {{Stier|4}}: {{Green|2.12%}} ({{Green|1}}/{{Yellow|47.23}})

== Usage ==
=== Upgrading ===
A '''Transmission Tuner''' can be combined in an {{Item|Anvil}} with any item with a {{AN|Transmission}} ability, upgrading its range by {{Green|1}} block. Up to {{Item|Transmission Tuner|amount=4}}s can be applied to an item, boosting its teleport range by up to {{Green|4}} blocks.

The following items can have '''Transmission Tuners''' applied to them:
* {{Item|Aspect of the End}}
* {{Item|Aspect of the Void}}
* {{Item|Etherwarp Conduit}}
* {{Item|Sinseeker Scythe}}

=== Crafting ===
{{Crafting Usage}}

Note that the {{Item|Aspect of the Leech (Uncommon)}} can only be upgraded '''once''' with '''Transmission Tuners''': it can be further upgraded using {{Item|Super Leech Modifier|amount=2}}s.

== Trivia ==
* Despite {{AN|Shadow Warp}} and {{AN|Wither Impact}} teleporting the player, neither abilities can be upgraded with '''Transmission Tuners''' due to not having the word {{AN|Transmission}} in their name.
* '''Transmission Tuners''' used to be bugged, boosting the range of {{AN|Transmission}} abilities by {{Green|2}} blocks: this also made it applicable only twice, up to {{Green|4}} blocks.
